## Sweep-5 — what actually changed (supersedes cont-22 § 4)

The corpus was measured before and after over all 85 specs, per-spec. The counts and
the delta live in the durable receipt — PR #2205's body and commit `d915b42d6` — not
here: `.session-notes` is memory-only and carries no verified figures
(`burn-down-reporting.md` MUST-3). Re-derive by running the tool per-spec over
`specs/*.md`; do NOT use `--all` (see Traps).

Two scanner defects, both fixed in PR #2205:

- **The Tier-2 coverage scan read ONE test root** (`<root>/tests/integration`). This
  repo has NINE; the other eight are `packages/*/tests/integration`. kailash-ml keeps
  all 82 of its Tier-2 tests there. **Every one of the 18 coverage gaps was this.**
- **`ClassName.member` citations resolved to zero candidate FILES**, because the
  resolver looked for a MODULE named e.g. `FeatureField`. Now resolved against an AST
  class index that walks methods, nested classes, plain assignments AND `AnnAssign` —
  the last being how every dataclass field is spelled, and the largest single source.

Resolution is member-by-member and cannot pass by blanket suppression: an absent member
on a real class, and an absent class, both still orphan. Three regression tests, each
paired with a control; the two fix-dependent ones were verified to FAIL against the
pre-fix tool.

